{"name":"Caramelise","hex":"#d58a37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caramelise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of caramelize."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caramelise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caramelization","blocks":[{"text":"Caramelization is a process of browning of sugar used extensively in cooking for the resulting butter-like flavor and brown color. The brown colors are produced by three groups of polymers: caramelans (C24H36O18), caramelens (C36H50O25), and caramelins (C125H188O80). As the process occurs, volatile chemicals such as diacetyl (known for its intense butter-like taste) are released, producing the characteristic caramel flavor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/2014_0531_Cr%C3%A8me_br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e_Doi_Mae_Salong.jpg/330px-2014_0531_Cr%C3%A8me_br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e_Doi_Mae_Salong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caramelization","wikidata":"Q73185"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Teilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png/500px-Teilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Teilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png/1280px-Teilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Teilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png/500px-Teilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A partially caramelized lump of sugar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeilweise_karamellisierter_W%C3%BCrfelzucker.png"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Caramel Custard Dessert